[statement]
apk sorts the request's names ignoring ASCII case, and byte by byte where
that ties, and walks them in that order: `a`, `Ab`, `aB`, `ab`, `B`, `c`,
where byte order would put `Ab` and `B` first.

[repository]
P:B
V:1

P:Ab
V:1

P:a
V:1

P:aB
V:1

P:c
V:1

P:ab
V:1

[request]
c
aB
B
ab
a
Ab

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install a 1
install Ab 1
install aB 1
install ab 1
install B 1
install c 1
